/* book: lead: A state variable is a signal that holds part of a system's memory, such as a capacitor voltage, an inductor current, or a position and a velocity. An nth-order system needs n of them, collected in the state vector. The state model replaces one nth-order differential equation by n first-order equations, written in matrix form. This normal form is what computers integrate, and it is the starting poi */
